WEBVTT

00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:10.449
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Monday the twenty-fourth. Everyone on Teams? I've got seven little boxes and about three actual faces.</v>

00:00:12.380 --> 00:00:19.030
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah, here. Traffic on the ring road was ridiculous. Spent longer looking at the factory than getting into it.</v>

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:27.250
<v Sarah Okafor>Lovely start. Anyone's weekend plans survive the weather? Mine involved sitting outside, so obviously that didn't happen.</v>

00:00:27.809 --> 00:00:33.060
<v Grace Liu>We managed about ten minutes before the rain. Very British, eating under a garden umbrella.</v>

00:00:35.090 --> 00:00:39.990
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Sorry, was muted. Morning. Heard the rain bit, which probably covers the whole weekend.</v>

00:00:42.380 --> 00:00:48.329
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, before we get distracted completely, what's already finished? Keep that separate from what we're agreeing today.</v>

00:00:49.039 --> 00:00:53.240
<v Aisha Begum>Yeah so, finished the repair on the GT1 last night. That's done.</v>

00:00:55.329 --> 00:00:58.829
<v Tomasz Nowak>Good. That was the finished one in the handover, then.</v>

00:00:59.750 --> 00:01:06.750
<v Aisha Begum>Yep. And I signed off the inspection on the water system on Tuesday. That's historical as well, not something outstanding.</v>

00:01:07.819 --> 00:01:11.670
<v Fiona Doyle>Last Tuesday, yeah? Just making sure I'm reading the right bit.</v>

00:01:13.379 --> 00:01:15.480
<v Aisha Begum>Last Tuesday, yeah. Already signed off.</v>

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:23.420
<v Grace Liu>And I finished the repair on the Atlas last night. That's another completed one, nothing new off that.</v>

00:01:24.810 --> 00:01:27.260
<v Sarah Okafor>Fine, those stay in the done column.</v>

00:01:29.170 --> 00:01:36.170
<v Fiona Doyle>Only an observation from me: noticed the main conveyor was running a bit warm on nights but it settled down.</v>

00:01:37.909 --> 00:01:41.060
<v Tomasz Nowak>Settled back down, did it? Not still creeping up?</v>

00:01:42.909 --> 00:01:47.109
<v Fiona Doyle>No, it settled. I'm not raising a job for today off it.</v>

00:01:48.390 --> 00:01:56.439
<v Aisha Begum>Similar sort of thing, I heard a slight rattle from the Line 2 Safety Guard Interlock. Nothing to action yet, just an observation.</v>

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:01.700
<v Sarah Okafor>Understood. Neither of those is a new action this morning.</v>

00:02:02.069 --> 00:02:07.319
<v Aisha Begum>On the blocked stuff, the supplier still hasn't confirmed the delivery for the newer turbine.</v>

00:02:09.479 --> 00:02:13.680
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah, still blocked then. No new delivery date to put against it.</v>

00:02:16.099 --> 00:02:21.699
<v Aisha Begum>And still waiting on parts for the relief valve. Nothing we can do until they arrive.</v>

00:02:23.430 --> 00:02:28.330
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, both parked as blocked. Not pretending they're jobs we can get through today.</v>

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:40.550
<v Priya Raman>One more to keep off the list: we were going to replace the belt on the turbine one, but that's been pushed to next month, so ignore it.</v>

00:02:43.050 --> 00:02:45.500
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep, cancelled out of today's work. Thanks.</v>

00:02:46.580 --> 00:02:50.780
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, actual commitments now. What's the smaller inspection you've got in mind?</v>

00:02:53.219 --> 00:02:58.120
<v Aisha Begum>I'll inspect the power pack on one for leaks tomorrow. Low priority, that one.</v>

00:02:58.740 --> 00:03:02.240
<v Tomasz Nowak>Just the leak inspection, not rolling a repair into it?</v>

00:03:04.530 --> 00:03:09.430
<v Aisha Begum>Yeah, just inspect the power pack on one for leaks. That's what I'm taking.</v>

00:03:10.770 --> 00:03:12.870
<v Sarah Okafor>Cheers, Ash. Tomorrow, low priority. Clear.</v>

00:03:14.110 --> 00:03:22.509
<v Sarah Okafor>Priya Raman, can you sort the permit to work and isolation for the old turbine at half two? It matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:03:24.889 --> 00:03:30.490
<v Priya Raman>Yep, I'll sort the permit to work and isolation for the old turbine at half two.</v>

00:03:32.860 --> 00:03:38.460
<v Grace Liu>That's the permit and isolation we're talking about, rather than adding any turbine work onto it?</v>

00:03:40.849 --> 00:03:44.000
<v Priya Raman>Exactly. Permit to work and isolation, that's my bit.</v>

00:03:44.949 --> 00:03:50.900
<v Sarah Okafor>Good. It matters but it's not urgent, so no need to treat it as a drop-everything job.</v>

00:03:53.020 --> 00:04:00.370
<v Sarah Okafor>And safety Grace, can you write up the near miss at the pop valve for tomorrow at 9:30? Top priority please.</v>

00:04:01.960 --> 00:04:07.560
<v Grace Liu>Yes, I'll write up the near miss at the pop valve. Tomorrow at 9:30, top priority.</v>

00:04:09.879 --> 00:04:13.729
<v Fiona Doyle>Sorry, you clipped slightly there. Nine thirty tomorrow for the write-up?</v>

00:04:15.159 --> 00:04:16.910
<v Grace Liu>That's right, tomorrow at 9:30.</v>

00:04:18.660 --> 00:04:22.860
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks. That's the top-priority one, even though the due point is tomorrow.</v>

00:04:23.720 --> 00:04:30.720
<v Sarah Okafor>Ash, can you grease and check the bearings on the hot bearing? Not an emergency but don't let it slip.</v>

00:04:31.699 --> 00:04:37.300
<v Aisha Begum>Um, no, sorry, I can't take that one on. Don't put the hot bearing against me.</v>

00:04:38.240 --> 00:04:43.490
<v Tomasz Nowak>Fair enough. Boss, can you take the hot bearing instead, grease and check the bearings?</v>

00:04:45.120 --> 00:04:54.220
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah, I'll take it instead of Ash. I'll grease and check the bearings on the hot bearing. Not an emergency but don't let it slip, understood.</v>

00:04:56.480 --> 00:05:00.680
<v Fiona Doyle>And we haven't attached a particular time to that one, have we?</v>

00:05:02.120 --> 00:05:04.920
<v Sarah Okafor>No, no particular deadline agreed for that one.</v>

00:05:06.939 --> 00:05:11.139
<v Tomasz Nowak>There you go. Proof the boss does occasionally get out of Teams.</v>

00:05:13.199 --> 00:05:15.649
<v Sarah Okafor>Occasionally. Usually when somebody's hidden the charger.</v>

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:22.449
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah so, I'll update the risk assessment for work on the boiler safety valve tomorrow. Normal priority.</v>

00:05:24.769 --> 00:05:30.720
<v Grace Liu>Yep, separate from my near-miss write-up. Don't want those two getting muddled just because they're both paperwork.</v>

00:05:32.310 --> 00:05:37.560
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Exactly. Mine's the risk assessment for work on the boiler safety valve, normal priority, tomorrow.</v>

00:05:39.470 --> 00:05:41.220
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Mide. That one's yours.</v>

00:05:42.600 --> 00:05:46.800
<v Fiona Doyle>Two separate entries, then. Risk assessment normal priority; near-miss write-up top priority.</v>

00:05:48.339 --> 00:05:49.540
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yep, that's it.</v>

00:05:51.589 --> 00:05:54.389
<v Sarah Okafor>Any crossed wires on those before we finish?</v>

00:05:56.350 --> 00:06:01.250
<v Priya Raman>No, I'm clear. The old turbine, permit to work and isolation at half two.</v>

00:06:03.720 --> 00:06:09.670
<v Aisha Begum>And I've got the power pack on one for leaks tomorrow, low priority. Not the hot bearing.</v>

00:06:11.769 --> 00:06:17.019
<v Grace Liu>I'm clear too. The pop valve near miss written up tomorrow at 9:30, top priority.</v>

00:06:19.089 --> 00:06:22.589
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep, the hot bearing is with me now, not Ash.</v>

00:06:24.110 --> 00:06:29.709
<v Olumide Adeyemi>And the boiler safety valve risk assessment is with me for tomorrow, normal priority. All good.</v>

00:06:31.500 --> 00:06:38.500
<v Fiona Doyle>Blocked items stay blocked, finished stuff stays finished, and the belt replacement isn't on today's list. That all ties up.</v>

00:06:40.579 --> 00:06:44.430
<v Tomasz Nowak>Excellent. If only the ring road could organise itself that well.</v>

00:06:46.459 --> 00:06:49.959
<v Sarah Okafor>Wouldn't get your hopes up. Right, thanks everyone. That's us.</v>
